<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Krishnaraja Wodeyar III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1794–1868</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Krishnaraja Wodeyar III was maharaja of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> from 1799 to 1868. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a>'s defeat in 1799 the British placed him on the throne as a five-year-old, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diwan">diwan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/purnaiah">Purnaiah</a> governing. Following a peasant revolt in 1831 the British took over the administration, and he spent the rest of his reign as a patron of music, literature and the arts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/krishnaraja-wodeyar-iii.jpg" alt="Krishnaraja Wodeyar III" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Krishnaraja_Wadiyar_III,_Maharaja_of_Mysore.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
